the next k8s.gcr.io cutover attempt is at least two weeks out, so we should probably switch to the correct registry ahead of that.

@liggitt -- the plan was to search/replace these references and merge once the VDF was complete.
Without making these changes, a variety of container image upgrades ([debian base images as an example](https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/issues/58012)) would have been blocked on VDF, including some security-related ones (ref: https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/pull/91387).

While hiccups come with the territory in big shifts like this, VDF is almost three months past the initial target date, and a lot of PRs would've been blocked in the meantime w/o choosing the regional target.
